{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2130-06-07 16:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello Mr. Thompson, I'm Dr. Patel. I'll be part of your care team. You're here because of dizziness and unsteadiness again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2130-06-07 16:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I was doing okay after last time, but today I went for a walk and suddenly felt very woozy and fatigued."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2130-06-07 16:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You didn’t fall, but you didn’t feel safe walking. Any numbness, weakness, or vision changes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2130-06-07 16:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no numbness or vision problems. My wife says my right leg is dragging a bit, but I just notice my shoes make more noise when I walk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2130-06-07 16:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that’s important. Given your history of CNS lymphoma, we need to check if there’s any change in your brain lesions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2130-06-07 16:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had a PET scan after last discharge—was normal. Could this still be lymphoma?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2130-06-07 16:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The PET rules out systemic spread, but we still need an MRI to look closely at your brain. We’ll schedule that tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2130-06-07 16:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. I’ve been drinking more fluids—dry mouth lately—but no frequent urination."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2130-06-07 16:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll check your electrolytes. No fever, chills, or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2130-06-07 16:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, none of that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2130-06-07 16:55:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep monitoring. For now, just rest. A nurse will start your IV and draw some labs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2130-06-08 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your MRI from this morning shows the lesions in your brain have slightly increased in size, especially in the right occipital lobe and left internal capsule."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2130-06-08 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Increased? Does that mean the lymphoma is back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2130-06-08 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s concerning for recurrence. Other possibilities like methotrexate toxicity are less likely since your last dose was months ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2130-06-08 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s next? Another round of methotrexate?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2130-06-08 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re discussing with neuro-oncology. Given the progression, we’re planning to restart high-dose methotrexate, but at a higher dose—8 grams per square meter."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2130-06-08 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Higher dose? Is that safe?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2130-06-08 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll take precautions—urinary alkalinization and leucovorin rescue—to protect your kidneys and bone marrow. It’s a standard protocol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2130-06-08 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust you. When will it start?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2130-06-08 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Tomorrow, June 9th. We’ll admit you for close monitoring. We’ll also check your liver and kidney function closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2130-06-09 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Today’s the day for your methotrexate infusion. We’ve started IV fluids and sodium bicarbonate to protect your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2130-06-09 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. Any side effects I should watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2130-06-09 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor for nausea, mouth sores, and low blood counts. Your liver enzymes might rise temporarily, but we expect them to come down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2130-06-09 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the leucovorin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2130-06-09 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll start that 24 hours after the infusion ends. It helps ‘rescue’ your healthy cells from the chemo."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2130-06-09 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The infusion went smoothly. You tolerated it well. We’ll keep the fluids going and monitor your labs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2130-06-10 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your potassium is low—2.7 this morning. We’re giving you supplements through the IV and orally."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2130-06-10 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that from the fluids?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2130-06-10 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the aggressive hydration can flush out potassium. We’ll keep replacing it until it stabilizes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2130-06-10 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. My balance still feels off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2130-06-10 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We expected the dizziness to persist initially. We’re starting a short course of dexamethasone today—4 mg twice daily—to reduce brain swelling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2130-06-10 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Steroids? I’ve had them before. Will I gain weight again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2130-06-10 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "This is a low dose and short course—just until your next treatment. We’ll stop it before you go home to minimize side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2130-06-11 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your potassium is improving, up to 3.1. Your liver enzymes peaked yesterday but are starting to come down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2130-06-11 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my balance?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2130-06-11 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re walking more steadily today. The dexamethasone seems to be helping reduce the inflammation around the lesions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2130-06-11 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried I’d need a walker."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2130-06-11 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at all. You’re doing well. We’ll keep the dexamethasone for a few more days, then taper it off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2130-06-12 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning for discharge tomorrow. Your symptoms have improved, labs are trending better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2130-06-12 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What’s next for treatment?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2130-06-12 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get rituximab at the clinic next week. Then return here in two weeks for your next methotrexate dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2130-06-12 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need a port?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2130-06-12 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll place one during your next admission. It’ll make the infusions easier and protect your veins."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2130-06-12 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds like a plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2130-06-13 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared for discharge. Your dizziness has improved, potassium is normal, and you’re walking independently."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2130-06-13 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel much better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2130-06-13 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The MRI showed progression of lymphoma, but the treatment is working. You’ll continue with rituximab and methotrexate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2130-06-13 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And no more steroids at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2130-06-13 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Correct. We’ve stopped them. Just continue your aspirin and omeprazole. No magnesium citrate needed now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2130-06-13 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Patel. I appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2130-06-13 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. See you in the clinic next week. Call if you feel worse before then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2130-06-13 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2130-06-13 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "A nurse will go over your discharge instructions and medications before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2130-06-13 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright, I’m ready when they are."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2130-06-13 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. Thompson. We’re glad you’re feeling better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2130-06-13 10:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2130-06-13 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll see you soon for your next treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2130-06-13 10:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Looking forward to it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2130-06-13 10:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2130-06-13 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2130-06-07 16:43:00",
    "admission_end": "2130-06-13 18:12:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. Thompson, a male with a history of primary central nervous system lymphoma and prior systemic lymphoma, was readmitted due to worsening ataxia and dizziness. A repeat MRI showed increased enhancement in the right occipital lobe and left internal capsule, concerning for recurrent CNS lymphoma. He received a high-dose methotrexate infusion at 8 g/m² with urinary alkalinization and leucovorin rescue. He developed transient hypokalemia, managed with IV and oral supplementation, and was started on a short course of dexamethasone for symptom improvement. His condition stabilized, and he was discharged home with plans to continue rituximab and methotrexate therapy, including port placement at the next admission.",
    "problems": [
      "Other malignant lymphomas, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Lack of coordination",
      "Dizziness and giddiness",
      "Hypopotassemia",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Personal history of tuberculosis"
    ]
  }
}
